0..66 Comment "//! The body reads the carrier that a parameter\'s path type omits."
67..70 Comment "//!"
71..149 Comment "//! A parameter can write `Path(y, z)` and omit its carrier. The endpoints fix"
150..226 Comment "//! the carrier where the signature forms. A composite in the body reads the"
227..307 Comment "//! carrier from the type of its first path. So the body holds the hole that the"
308..329 Comment "//! signature solves."
330..333 Comment "//!"
334..412 Comment "//! The checker fills each hole that the signature solves in the declared type"
413..491 Comment "//! and in the body. The body then reads the carrier that the signature fixes."
492..564 Comment "//! A composite over the parameter meets the same composite in the type."
565..568 Comment "//!"
569..585 Comment "//! - see: #5272"
586..678 Comment "//! - see: `carrier-by-name.gandr` — a carrier supplied by name, and one omitted at a type"
680..755 Comment "/// A composite whose first path omits its carrier, at its own reflexivity."
